---
name: "Cloudflare Logpush over HTTPS → OCSF → Splunk"
description: |
  Receives Cloudflare Logpush batches on an HTTPS endpoint, normalizes the
  records to OCSF, and sends them to Splunk. Point a Logpush job with an HTTP
  destination at this endpoint, such as `https://tenzir.example.com:8443`.
  Logpush sends gzip-compressed, newline-delimited JSON and requires a
  trusted certificate.
---

accept_http "0.0.0.0:8443",
  tls={certfile: "/etc/tenzir/tls/cert.pem", keyfile: "/etc/tenzir/tls/key.pem"} {
  decompress_gzip
  read_ndjson
}
// Logpush validates a new destination with a test record.
where content? != "tests"
cloudflare::ocsf::normalize
to_splunk "https://splunk.example.com:8088",
  hec_token=secret("SPLUNK_HEC_TOKEN"),
  index="cloudflare"
